Usage: uget [options] <URL>

uget is a unicon utility for downlaoding files from the web. It supports
HTTP and HTTPS. If the protocol is not specified in the URL it defaults to HTTP,
(i,e unicon.org is equivalent to http://unicon.org)

Options:
	 -n : no https certificate verification
	 -o : overwrite existing file
	 -v : verbose output
	 -s : show http server response only, don't save the file
	 -p : print the content to the console, don't save to file
	 -r : maximum allowed redirects. Default to 3
	 -f : filename to save to. Default to the url filename
	 -6 : use ipv6
	 -h : show this help

